# Production build-time env for the marketing site.
#
# Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables into the client bundle when
# `next build` runs — they are NOT read at runtime. So this key MUST be present
# during the build; committing it here guarantees that on any platform. A real
# build-time env var of the same name (e.g. a per-environment key set by the
# deploy platform) overrides this file.
#
# The Turnstile SITE key is PUBLIC by design: it is rendered into the page HTML
# for the widget to load, and Cloudflare locks it to your allowed hostnames.
# Committing it is safe and standard.
#
# The matching SECRET key is NOT here — it lives only in the backend as
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY (server-side siteverify). Never put the secret in this repo.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAADzW2WXrzEE_SqCl
